id: pm-lifecycle-example-scope
title: Preserve explicit tracker scope in lifecycle recovery mutation examples
description: PR1608 CodeRabbit review4383854533 correctly identifies that block/unblock help retries retain the selected tracker but their rendered update examples drop bootstrap scope. Prefix each example with the canonical help retry bootstrap arguments and prove mutations cannot fall back to another tracker.
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,bug,review
created_at: "2026-10-27T00:30:40.690Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T00:35:37.836Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-27T00:35:37.075Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-27T00:35:37.075Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: A negative two-tracker control fails before the change and passes afterward; both block and unblock examples retain explicit tracker scope and extension suppression; the ambient tracker history stays unchanged; full required checks and review pass.
parent: pm-gh1607
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Prefix every rendered lifecycle mutation example with the selected tracker and explicit extension-suppression bootstrap arguments already retained by its inspection retry.
expected_result: Executing filled block/unblock examples from another working directory mutates only the explicitly selected tracker and retains extension suppression.
actual_result: "The unchanged implementation fails the new real-shell two-tracker control; the corrected implementation passes the full20-test linked cohort, complete typecheck, focused ESLint and docs links. Both trackers share the same item ID, and ambient history remains byte-for-byte semantically unchanged. Exact-head coverage, Windows and review remain pre-merge requirements."
